boards.prompt:
Use case: ui-mockup.
Asset type: practical ILBI mobile app concept board for choosing a design.
References: Image 1 is the ACTUAL ILBI logo symbol: black lowercase i/dot, blue flowing vertical ribbon and curved black bowl. Copy this recognizable existing symbol faithfully, do not invent a logo. Image 2 is the real desktop dark theme, Image 3 the real desktop light theme. Adapt their BRAND and PALETTE to mobile, not their wide desktop layout. A proper small logo symbol, optionally with the actual lowercase wordmark "ilbi.uz", must appear in app headers, document lists and receipt branding; NEVER substitute uppercase plain "ILBI" text. In dark mode lighten only the black logo parts to bone white as in desktop, retain the blue ribbon. Do not place a white square behind the dark-mode logo.
Composition: landscape 1536x1024 or higher practical resolution, exactly THREE fully visible straight upright modern phone mockups, equal scale, generous gaps on a very quiet neutral studio backdrop. Front-facing, almost no perspective. Modern discreet camera cutouts, realistic status bar, safe areas. Large sharp readable Uzbek Latin labels, tabular aligned amounts in so'm, no gibberish, no watermarks. These are static design proposals, not real screenshots or performance benchmarks.
Palette is deliberately BLACK / WARM WHITE from the desktop. Light: warm bone #F0EFEB app background, white surfaces, near-black #0B0909 text and primary buttons, bone-white button text. Dark: #0B0909 app background, graphite #171515/#1A1818 surfaces, bone #F0EFEB text and primary buttons with black text. Fine muted dividers and secondary gray. Blue ONLY in the actual brand logo, not in primary buttons, selected tabs, form borders or decorative charts. Use tiny restrained green/amber/red status accents only where meaningful, always with text/icon. No gradients, blur, neon, decorative charts, large floating cards, excessive shadows or empty decorative space.
Mobile minimalism: flat list rows with thin dividers, no separate tall card for every cart item; compact header; one short customer row; numbers aligned; minimum practical tap areas ~44pt. Image size and visual density are independent from touch target size. In CARTS product thumbnails, if shown at all, must be TINY 24–28pt squares, never large product photos or banners. Alternative text-only carts have no photos and no empty image placeholders. No duplicate persistent menu.
Navigation retained: exactly five bottom tabs with icon + text: "Bosh", "Tovar", "Savdo", "Qarz", "Menyu". Root header has top-left hamburger; it and bottom Menyu open the SAME LEFT slide-in drawer. Detail screen has back arrow. Selected tab black/bone, not blue. Sticky primary action ABOVE navbar. Focus sheets may dim background; normal page content and controls stay inside phone. Keep the visual hierarchy practical, restrained, calm and usable. Small non-blocking press and check feedback may be suggested, never confetti or blocking splashes.
All people, transactions, document data and drawn signatures are synthetic demonstrations. A drawn-signature UI is labelled "Qo'lda imzo"; do not claim certified cryptographic signing, E-IMZO validation or legal verification.

Primary request: THREE genuinely compact cart layout alternatives side by side, all with same data. Outside heading "16 — IXCHAM SAVAT". Compare density and usability, not giant pictures.
Sample cart has TEN product types, FIFTEEN sale units, grand total 160 000 so'm. Rows:
"Sut 1 L" 2 × 11 500 = 23 000;
"Non" 3 × 4 000 = 12 000;
"Suv 1.5 L" 2 × 5 000 = 10 000;
"Shakar 1 kg" 1 × 16 000 = 16 000;
"Choy 100 g" 1 × 18 000 = 18 000;
"Yog' 1 L" 1 × 22 000 = 22 000;
"Guruch 1 kg" 2 × 15 000 = 30 000;
"Tuxum (10 dona)" 1 × 18 000 = 18 000;
"Tuz 1 kg" 1 × 3 000 = 3 000;
"Makaron 500 g" 1 × 8 000 = 8 000.
Show at least EIGHT readable rows, with scrolling clearly allowing access to remaining rows, ideally all ten if space allows without tiny text. Total includes every row even if last two are below fold. Header "Savat", summary "10 tur · 15 dona", short customer row "Ali Valiyev". Row layout is name + small "quantity × actual unit price" and right-aligned line total. Tapping unit price or quantity allows editing; no large repeated steppers until row is selected. Use a compact search or add-item control. Pinned grand total "160 000 so'm", single main "To'lovga o'tish", bottom Savdo selected. Actual customer price is shown; catalog prices or cost are not mixed into every row.

Phone 1 caption "A · Kichik rasm": light warm-white theme, TINY 24–28pt thumbnails aligned to product names. Flat 48–56pt rows, at least eight visible. Images are only quiet recognition aids; text and numbers dominate. No oversized customer card, no giant product rows. Actual proper logo small in top bar.
Phone 2 caption "B · Rasmsiz jadval": light theme, completely photo-free compact text rows. Clear subtle column headings "Tovar", "Soni × Narxi", "Jami". Use two compact lines per row where necessary; prioritize at least eight readable rows, with aligned tabular numbers and thin separators. One selected milk row has a small pencil next to 11 500, no oversized editing panel. Do not add empty photo placeholders.
Phone 3 caption "C · Tungi jadval": same efficient photo-free layout in desktop graphite/bone dark palette. White/bone primary checkout button, tiny blue-ribbon actual logo in header, all other UI monochrome. At least eight readable rows. Do not invert every other row or add bright panels. All three totals 160 000, same actual prices and same bottom nav.

